EVERY PRIMARY DEX OPCODE.

One numbered entry for every primary byte from 0x00 through 0xff.
Standard profile: DEX 035, 037, 038, 039, 040 and experimental 041.
Earlier archival 009/013 formats and future revisions are not granted here.
The 32 unused bytes have entries but no invented executable meaning.

Read the sibling machine, formats and shared-effects documents together
with each entry. Uppercase named rules in Validity, such as FRAME or FIELD,
refer to "Validity arithmetic and shared effects.english". B, F, D and C
are the authoritative URLs named in README.md; source snapshot identities
are in fixtures/dex/sources/manifest.tsv. Each mnemonic identifies an entry;
it does not stand in for that entry's English operation. Sentences were
authored as complete operations, not assembled from a verb/noun grammar.
The TSV has the same operation paragraphs and structured metadata.

ENTRY 001 — 0x00 — NOP.

Identification: nop.
Encoding: 10x; ØØ:op; 1 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Leave the method's registers and heap unchanged. Continue at the following code unit. A payload identifier whose low byte is zero is data, not this operation.

Reads: none.
Changes: none.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 1 code unit.
Operand and contextual validity: The full executable code unit is 0x0000.
Exceptional completion: No instruction-specific synchronous exception.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x00 nop; F: 10x; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0x26; 0x2b; 0x2c.

ENTRY 002 — 0x01 — MOVE.

Identification: move.
Encoding: 12x; B:A:op; 1 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Copy the thirty-two non-reference bits in source register B into destination register A, without converting an integer to a float or a float to an integer.

Reads: vB.
Changes: vA.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 1 code unit.
Operand and contextual validity: A and B are four-bit indices. FRAME; TYPES.
Exceptional completion: No instruction-specific synchronous exception after successful verification.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x01 move; F: 12x; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0x02; 0x03; 0x07.

ENTRY 003 — 0x02 — MOVE/FROM16.

Identification: move/from16.
Encoding: 22x; AA:op BBBB; 2 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Read the non-reference word in the register selected by the sixteen-bit source index. Place the same thirty-two bits in the register selected by the eight-bit destination index.

Reads: vB.
Changes: vA.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 2 code units.
Operand and contextual validity: A is eight bits and B is sixteen bits. FRAME; TYPES.
Exceptional completion: No instruction-specific synchronous exception after successful verification.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x02 move/from16; F: 22x; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0x01; 0x03.

ENTRY 004 — 0x03 — MOVE/16.

Identification: move/16.
Encoding: 32x; ØØ:op AAAA BBBB; 3 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Copy the original non-reference thirty-two-bit source word to the destination, using the two full sixteen-bit register indices. The extra encoding space changes which registers can be named, not the copied value.

Reads: vB.
Changes: vA.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 3 code units.
Operand and contextual validity: A and B are sixteen-bit indices. FRAME; TYPES.
Exceptional completion: No instruction-specific synchronous exception after successful verification.
