ENTRY 005 — 0x04 — MOVE-WIDE.

Identification: move-wide.
Encoding: 12x; B:A:op; 1 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Read both words of source pair B before writing either word of destination pair A. Copy the entire sixty-four-bit value unchanged. Overlap by one register is permitted and must not corrupt the value being copied.

Reads: vB; vB+1.
Changes: vA; vA+1.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 1 code unit.
Operand and contextual validity: Four-bit pair starts. FRAME; PAIRS; TYPES.
Exceptional completion: No instruction-specific synchronous exception after successful verification.
