ENTRY 015 — 0x0e — RETURN-VOID.

Identification: return-void.
Encoding: 10x; ØØ:op; 1 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Complete this void method normally without supplying a return value. Leave this invocation and resume its caller under the method-exit rules.

Reads: method frame and monitor state.
Changes: caller continuation; current frame removed.
Execution index: Return to caller; do not advance within this method.
Operand and contextual validity: RETURN: method prototype returns void; constructor and monitor obligations hold.
Exceptional completion: EXIT rules, including monitor discipline; no data result is produced.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x0e return-void; F: 10x; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
