ENTRY 030 — 0x1d — MONITOR-ENTER.

Identification: monitor-enter.
Encoding: 11x; AA:op; 1 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Read the non-null object reference in A and acquire that object's monitor for the current thread. Wait if another thread owns it. Reentry by the owner increments its hold count; a first acquisition establishes the monitor synchronization ordering.

Reads: reference vA; monitor ownership.
Changes: monitor ownership and hold count.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 1 code unit.
Operand and contextual validity: FRAME; initialized object reference; MONITOR verification rules.
Exceptional completion: NullPointerException for null. Acquisition and runtime asynchronous-exception behavior are separate from ordinary register effects.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x1d monitor-enter; F: 11x; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0x1e.

ENTRY 031 — 0x1e — MONITOR-EXIT.

Identification: monitor-exit.
Encoding: 11x; AA:op; 1 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Release one hold by the current thread on the monitor of the object in A. When the count reaches zero, make the monitor available to another thread and apply release ordering. Leave the reference register unchanged.

Reads: reference vA; monitor ownership.
Changes: monitor hold count and possibly ownership.
Execution index: On success current + 1; on exception use current + 1 for attribution and handler search.
Operand and contextual validity: FRAME; MONITOR; current thread must own the monitor.
Exceptional completion: NullPointerException for null; IllegalMonitorStateException for nonownership. Attribute an exception as if the execution index had already advanced past this instruction.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x1e monitor-exit; F: 11x; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0x1d.

ENTRY 032 — 0x1f — CHECK-CAST.

Identification: check-cast.
Encoding: 21c; AA:op BBBB; 2 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Check whether the reference in A is compatible with referenced type B. For an admissible reference type, null passes; an incompatible non-null object throws ClassCastException. On success retain the same register bits while refining the verifier's type knowledge.

Reads: reference vA; type_ids[B].
Changes: no changed reference bits; verifier type narrowed.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 2 code units.
Operand and contextual validity: FRAME; valid type index; initialized reference. TYPE-CHECK discrepancy: the public table discusses primitive targets, while the inspected ART verifier rejects primitive and void targets.
Exceptional completion: ClassCastException for an incompatible non-null reference; RESOLUTION. Primitive-target behavior is not granted as verified executable code; see audit.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0x1f check-cast; F: 21c; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0x20.

ENTRY 033 — 0x20 — INSTANCE-OF.

Identification: instance-of.
Encoding: 22c; B:A:op CCCC; 2 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 035,037,038,039,040,041.

Test the object in B against reference type C and write one to A if it is an instance, otherwise zero. Null yields zero. Do not cast, modify or initialize the tested object.

