ENTRY 251 — 0xfa — INVOKE-POLYMORPHIC.

Identification: invoke-polymorphic.
Encoding: 45cc; A:G:op BBBB F:E:D:C HHHH; 4 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 038,039,040,041.

Invoke signature-polymorphic method B on the selected receiver, using prototype H as the actual call-site argument and return signature. Read the remaining selected words as arguments. MethodHandle.invoke permits its defined adaptations; invokeExact requires an exact method type. A matching move-result may retain a normal returned value.

Reads: selected receiver and arguments C,D,E,F,G; method_ids[B]; proto_ids[H].
Changes: callee effects; pending result on normal return.
Execution index: Enter target; normal continuation current + 4; otherwise exception transfer.
Operand and contextual validity: DEX 038 or later; COUNT-LIST; INVOCATION; B must denote a supported signature-polymorphic method, not an arbitrary virtual method; argument count includes receiver.
Exceptional completion: RESOLUTION; NullPointerException for null receiver; signature API exceptions including WrongMethodTypeException and adaptation ClassCastException when applicable; arbitrary target exceptions.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0xfa invoke-polymorphic; F: 45cc; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
