ENTRY 252 — 0xfb — INVOKE-POLYMORPHIC/RANGE.

Identification: invoke-polymorphic/range.
Encoding: 4rcc; AA:op BBBB CCCC HHHH; 4 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 038,039,040,041.

Read a consecutive receiver-and-argument interval beginning at C and invoke signature-polymorphic method B under the call-site prototype H. Apply that method's exact or adapting invocation rules rather than inferring the signature from the generic declaration. Make a normal return value available to the next matching move-result.

Reads: vC through vC+A−1; method_ids[B]; proto_ids[H].
Changes: callee effects; pending result.
Execution index: Enter target; normal continuation current + 4; otherwise exception transfer.
Operand and contextual validity: DEX 038 or later; COUNT-RANGE; signature-polymorphic method and prototype validity; INVOCATION.
Exceptional completion: RESOLUTION; null receiver gives NullPointerException; signature-method API exceptions and arbitrary invoked-target exceptions.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0xfb invoke-polymorphic/range; F: 4rcc; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0xfa; 0x0a–0x0c.

ENTRY 253 — 0xfc — INVOKE-CUSTOM.

Identification: invoke-custom.
Encoding: 35c; A:G:op BBBB F:E:D:C; 3 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 038,039,040,041.

Resolve call site B, invoking its bootstrap linker when no CallSite is already associated. Use the first associated CallSite if concurrent resolution wins. Invoke that site's MethodHandle target with the selected argument words as an exact invocation of the requested call-site type. Retain any normal value only through the next matching move-result.

Reads: call_site_ids[B]; bootstrap metadata; selected C,D,E,F,G argument words.
Changes: call-site association; bootstrap and target effects; pending result.
Execution index: Resolve and enter target; normal continuation current + 3; otherwise exception transfer.
Operand and contextual validity: DEX 038 or later; COUNT-LIST; valid call-site metadata and argument prototype. No implicit receiver is added; a receiver needed by the target is an explicit parameter.
Exceptional completion: BootstrapMethodError wraps a bootstrap-linker exception and also signals a non-CallSite return, null target or wrong target type. RESOLUTION and arbitrary target exceptions remain distinct.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0xfc invoke-custom; F: 35c; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0xfd; 0xfa; 0x0a–0x0c.

ENTRY 254 — 0xfd — INVOKE-CUSTOM/RANGE.

Identification: invoke-custom/range.
Encoding: 3rc; AA:op BBBB CCCC; 3 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 038,039,040,041.

Resolve the indicated dynamic call site and invoke its associated target with the consecutive argument words beginning at C. Reuse an already associated CallSite, including one first installed by another thread. The target is called with the exact requested call-site method type, and a normal result is offered to a subsequent matching move-result.

Reads: call_site_ids[B]; bootstrap metadata; vC through vC+A−1.
Changes: call-site association; bootstrap and callee effects; pending result.
Execution index: Resolve and enter target; normal continuation current + 3; otherwise exception transfer.
Operand and contextual validity: DEX 038 or later; COUNT-RANGE; call-site metadata and argument type checks; no automatically inserted receiver.
Exceptional completion: BootstrapMethodError under the same bootstrap/target-validation conditions as 0xfc; RESOLUTION; arbitrary invoked-target exceptions.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0xfd invoke-custom/range; F: 3rc; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0xfc; 0xfb.

ENTRY 255 — 0xfe — CONST-METHOD-HANDLE.

Identification: const-method-handle.
Encoding: 21c; AA:op BBBB; 2 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 039,040,041.

Resolve the method-handle entry selected by B and place its MethodHandle object reference in A. The entry's handle kind selects a field or method operation, but loading the handle does not itself perform that operation or invoke its target.

Reads: method_handles[B]; member resolution context.
Changes: reference vA; resolution/allocation state.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 2 code units.
Operand and contextual validity: DEX 039 or later; FRAME; valid method-handle table index and referenced member kind/access.
Exceptional completion: RESOLUTION errors for referenced members or types; OutOfMemoryError may prevent materializing the handle.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0xfe const-method-handle; F: 21c; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0xfa; 0xff.

ENTRY 256 — 0xff — CONST-METHOD-TYPE.

Identification: const-method-type.
Encoding: 21c; AA:op BBBB; 2 code unit(s).
Validity class: standard. Applicable versions: 039,040,041.

Resolve prototype B to a MethodType object describing its return and parameter types, and place that object's reference in A. No method is called and no argument registers are read.

Reads: proto_ids[B]; referenced type information.
Changes: reference vA; resolution/allocation state.
Execution index: On normal completion continue at current + 2 code units.
Operand and contextual validity: DEX 039 or later; FRAME; valid prototype index and referenced types.
Exceptional completion: RESOLUTION of component types; OutOfMemoryError may prevent obtaining the MethodType.
Sources: B: Summary of bytecode set, 0xff const-method-type; F: 21c; D: code_item and version history; C: applicable validity constraints; ART-LIST; SMALI.
Related: 0xfe; 0xfa.
